            <div xml:id="ch6subch1">

                <pb facs="0391" n="379" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg379"/>

                <head>I. Repeal of sections 2, 3, and 6 of the Neutrality Act by law approved
                    November 17, 1941<anchor n="2" xml:id="ch6subch1-f1"/>
                </head>
                <p>[For views of the President and the Secretary of State regarding repeal of
                    Sections 2, 3, and 6 of the Neutrality Act of 1939, see the following:</p>
                <p>Message of the President to Congress, October 9, 1941, Department of State <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, October 11, 1941, page 257.</p>
                <p>Statement by the Secretary of State before the Committee on Foreign Affairs of
                    the House of Representatives, released October 13, 1941, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ibid.</hi>, October 18, 1941, page 291.</p>
                <p>Statement by the Secretary of State before the Senate Foreign Relations
                    Committee, October 21, 1941, <hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, October 25,
                    1941, page 307.</p>
                <p>Letter addressed by the President to the Speaker and the Majority Leader of the
                    House of Representatives, <hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, November 15, 1941,
                    page 379.</p>
                <p>Letter addressed by the Secretary of State to the Speaker and the Majority Leader
                    of the House of Representatives, November 13, 1941, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ibid.</hi>, page 380.]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
